.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fP, \fB\-\-input\fP \fIfile\fP[\fB:\fP\fIkey=value...\fP]
An xy data file to plot, with optional colon-separated overrides
\fBsymbol=\fP, \fBfill=\fP, \fBpen=\fP, \fBdelimiter=\fP, \fBxexpr=\fP,
\fByexpr=\fP (see DESCRIPTION). Repeatable; required at least once.
.TP
.B \-O\fP, \fB\-\-output\fP \fIroot\fP
Output root name. Default: the first \fB\-\-input\fP file's basename
with its extension removed.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIfmt\fP
Output format passed to \fBgmt figure\fP: \fBpdf\fP, \fBpng\fP,
\fBps\fP, \fBjpg\fP, \fBtif\fP, \fBeps\fP, ... Default \fBpdf\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-title \fItext\fP
Plot title, placed above the frame.
.TP
.B \-\-xlabel \fItext\fP, \fB\-\-ylabel \fItext\fP
Axis labels. Only used for a linear/Cartesian projection (an auto-fit
default, or an explicit \fB\-Jx\fP/\fB\-JX\fP); a geographic or other
map projection has no per-axis label, matching \fBmbm_xyplot\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-dpi \fIdpi\fP
The final raster's resolution (via \fBgmt figure\fP).
.TP
.B \-X\fP, \fB\-\-execute
Run the generated script immediately after writing it.
.TP
.B \-V\fP, \fB\-\-verbose
Print the generated script's path and a one-line summary.
.TP
.B \-R\fP, \fB\-\-region \fIxmin/xmax/ymin/ymax\fP[\fIr\fP]
Plot region. Fields may be given as \fIdd:mm:ss\fP. A trailing \fBr\fP
means the four values are two corner points (southwest, northeast)
rather than a w/e/s/n range; a bare \fBr\fP reformats the
auto-computed data bounds into that corner-point form. Default: computed
from the data itself.
.TP
.B \-J\fP, \fB\-\-projection \fIspec\fP
GMT map scale/projection spec, e.g. \fBx0.02\fP (linear, 0.02 inch/unit),
\fBm1.0\fP (Mercator, 1 inch/degree). Default: an auto-fit linear
projection with independent x and y scales (see DESCRIPTION), chosen to
fill the page.
.TP
.B \-P\fP, \fB\-\-pagesize \fIsize\fP
Page size code: \fBa\fP\-\fBf\fP, \fBe1\fP (US sizes), \fBa0\fP\-\fBa10\fP,
\fBb0\fP\-\fBb10\fP, \fBc0\fP\-\fBc7\fP (ISO/architectural), or \fBm1\fP\-\fBm6\fP
(large-format). Default \fBa\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-portrait\fP, \fB\-\-landscape
Force the page orientation instead of choosing automatically; when
neither is given, this auto-fit independent-scale mode defaults to
landscape, matching \fBmbm_xyplot\fP/\fBmbm_histplot\fP.
.TP
.B \-B\fP, \fB\-\-tick\-info \fIspec\fP
Raw \fB\-B\fP basemap tick-interval spec, overriding the automatically
computed one.
.TP
.B \-\-length\-scale \fIspec\fP
A GMT distance (map) scale bar spec, passed as \fB\-L\fP\fIspec\fP on
\fBgmt basemap\fP, e.g. \fBfx10/2/32.70/5.0+lkm\fP (\fBmbm_xyplot\fP's
\fB\-MGL\fP). The literal word \fBcenter\fP appearing between two
slashes is replaced with the plot's own data center (e.g.
\fBfxcenter/5.0+lkm\fP), matching \fBmbm_xyplot\fP's own substitution.
.TP
.B \-S\fP, \fB\-\-symbol \fIsymbol\fP
Default GMT symbol code and size for every \fB\-\-input\fP file that
does not set its own \fBsymbol=\fP, e.g. \fBc0.1\fP (circle, 0.1 inch).
Default: none (points are connected with a line instead).
.TP
.B \-G\fP, \fB\-\-fill \fIcolor\fP
Default symbol/polygon fill color for every \fB\-\-input\fP file that
does not set its own \fBfill=\fP. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-W\fP, \fB\-\-pen \fIpen\fP
Default line pen for every \fB\-\-input\fP file that does not set its
own \fBpen=\fP, e.g. \fB1p,black\fP. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-coast
Enable a coastline overlay (\fBgmt coast\fP), drawn \fIafter\fP the xy
data plots and \fIbefore\fP text labels and the basemap frame, matching
\fBmbm_xyplot\fP's own layer order exactly (data points that fall on a
solid land fill are covered by it, just as in the classic macro).
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-resolution \fI{f,h,i,l,c}\fP
Coastline database resolution: full, high, intermediate, low, crude.
Default \fBf\fP when \fB\-\-coast\fP is enabled with no other coastline
option given.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill \fIcolor\fP
Fill colors for land, water, and lakes. \fB\-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP
defaults to \fB200\fP (a mid-gray) when \fB\-\-coast\fP is enabled with
no fill, pen, river, or boundary option given at all -- an
\fBmbm_xyplot\fP-specific default with no equivalent in
\fBmbm_grdplot\fP/\fBmbpy_grdplot\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-river \fIcolor\fP
Draw rivers in the given color.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-boundary \fIspec\fP
Draw a national boundary; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-pen \fIpen\fP
Pen for the coastline itself. Defaults to \fB1p\fP together with the
\fB\-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP default described above.
.TP
.B \-\-text \fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP
Place a text label (\fBgmt text\fP), e.g.
\fB\-122.2/36.6/12/0/1/LB/Monterey Bay\fP. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-gmt\-default \fIparam/value\fP
Override a GMT default parameter for this plot (e.g.
\fBMAP_FRAME_TYPE/plain\fP); repeatable.

.SH EXAMPLES
Plot a single time series of sensor depth values as a thin connecting
line, rendered directly to a PNG:

.br
 mbpy_xyplot \-I "depth_vs_time.txt:pen=0.5p,blue" \-O depth_ts \\
.br
     \-\-title "Sensor Depth vs Time" \-\-xlabel "Time (s)" \\
.br
     \-\-ylabel "Sensor Depth (m)" \\
.br
     \-\-pagesize b \-\-landscape \-\-format png \-\-dpi 150 \-\-execute \-V

Plot navigation fixes from a comma-delimited file (selecting the
longitude and latitude columns explicitly) as symbols, with a
coastline underlay:

.br
 mbpy_xyplot \-I "fixes.csv:delimiter=,:xexpr=c[2]:yexpr=c[3]:symbol=c0.05:fill=red" \\
.br
     \-O fixes_plot \-\-title "Vehicle Fixes" \\
.br
     \-\-coast \-\-coast\-resolution i \\
.br
     \-\-format png \-\-execute \-V

Plot two data files together, one as a line and one as symbols, over a
user-specified region:

.br
 mbpy_xyplot \-I "reference.xy:pen=1p,black" \\
.br
     \-I "observed.xy:symbol=c0.08:fill=red" \\
.br
     \-O comparison \-R "\-10/110/\-5/55" \\
.br
     \-\-title "Reference vs Observed" \-\-format pdf \-V

